@startuml
title Exact multi-shooting artillery probability sequence
autonumber
actor User
participant "Artillery View" as View
participant "Artillery Controller" as Controller
participant "calculate_artillery" as Resolver
participant "ArtilleryRulesRegistry" as Registry
participant "Finite probability distribution" as Distribution

User -> View : enter ArtilleryCommand facts
View -> Registry : available_unit_rules(Shooting Nation, initial Range In)
Registry --> View : eligible declared Unit-rule options
View -> Controller : calculate_artillery_use_case(command, registry)
Controller -> Resolver : calculate_artillery(command, registry)
Resolver -> Registry : for_nation(command.shooting_nation)
Registry --> Resolver : nation policy
Resolver -> Distribution : initialize one input state with probability 1

loop Shooting #1 through horizon
  alt Shooting #1
    Resolver -> Distribution : apply initial Range In 1/2/3 To Hit + gun-count and nation rules
  else Shooting #2+
    Resolver -> Distribution : apply Repeat To Hit using retained point and spotter LOS
    Resolver -> Distribution : apply Repeat successful-save re-roll
  end
  Distribution -> Distribution : per covered Team: miss / hit survives / hit destroyed
  Distribution -> Distribution : update pin, team counts, leader and prior-loss state
  Distribution --> Resolver : merged exact state probabilities
  Resolver -> Resolver : summarize this shooting row
  opt another shooting remains in horizon
    Resolver -> Distribution : Rally transition (if pinned)
    Resolver -> Distribution : Unit Good Spirits / Last Stand transition
    Resolver -> Distribution : Formation Last Stand transition when requested
    Distribution --> Resolver : Starting Step state probabilities
  end
end

Resolver --> Controller : ArtilleryResult with ShootingResult per shooting
Controller --> View : result
View --> User : exact distributions / morale / pin / destruction outputs

note over Resolver,Distribution
No random die draws or Monte Carlo trials occur.
Transitions use exact rational-derived probabilities and merge equal states.
The horizon is a user-selected project bound, not a V4 maximum.
end note

note right of Distribution
ToT on a Repeat is rejected because the rule interaction is unresolved.
Other nation/weapon rules and changes to roster/In-Command status
between turns are outside the current model.
end note
@enduml
